Patches to the wasip3 Go fork (scripts/bootstrap-go-wasip3.sh's commit) for
Go's own commands, built by clis/go.toml, go-compile.toml, go-asm.toml and
go-link.toml. Applied by clis/patches/patch-go.sh.

- cmd/go runs compile, asm and link through eryx:process/run (a WASI command
  can't start another), as go-compile, go-asm and go-link:
  cmd/go/internal/work/exec_wasip3.go, and the binding in
  internal/eryx/process.
- internal/wasi: cabi_realloc allocates from an arena during that call. A Go
  heap allocation while the host is in the middle of a long import can crash
  the runtime when a GC cycle is under way.
- cmd/internal/objabi: the tools' -V output names them compile, asm and link,
  without the go- prefix, as cmd/go expects.
- cmd/go's file locks are no-ops (WASI has none), and it keeps no telemetry
  counters and starts no upload process.

